  "question_id": "step-exact",
  "new_explanation": "The exact solution is y(t)=2 exp(-t) for this initial condition and rate, so y(1)=2/e. The expression 2 - 1 ignores that the slope depends on y. It is neither the exact solution at t=1 nor the one-step forward-Euler result with h=1, which is 2-2=0.",
  "reasoning": "For y-prime=-y and y(0)=2, the exact value at t=1 is 2/e. One forward Euler step of h=1 uses slope -2 at t=0 and gives 2+1*(-2)=0. Subtracting the constant one is neither of those results. The corrected explanation states these distinctions accurately.",
  "course_json_changed_fields": [
    "$.items[1].explanation"
  ],
  "raw_byte_inverse_exact_for_course_and_embedded_html": true,
